 "id": "2026-10-27-typhoon-infa-intensifies",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Typhoon In-fa gained sixty miles an hour in one day. Where is it heading?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Monday, the Joint Typhoon Warning Center says, In-fa leapt from a category one to a category four storm within hours. Winds rose from ninety to one hundred thirty miles an hour. Warm water and favorable conditions drove the surge, the center says."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then it nearly stalled, held between two high pressure ridges, the Guam service says. On Tuesday afternoon, the National Weather Service in Guam put In-fa about eleven hundred sixty-five miles east of Guam, creeping at two miles an hour, with winds of one hundred twenty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The Joint Typhoon Warning Center forecasts a super typhoon by Thursday, passing near Pagan Island in the northern Marianas on Friday. Saipan sits just outside the forecast cone. No watches or warnings were in effect Tuesday morning."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will In-fa pass north of Saipan? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
